[Event "Wizard Opening"]
[StudyName "Wizard Opening"]
[ChapterName "Early Qxd2: Kxd2 and Qxf7"]
[Variant "Antichess"]
[Result "*"]
[Annotator "Adapted from Dy1ar’s Lichess study f3NuTHGo"]

{ Train as White. Replay this line from the initial position. }
1. c4 d5 2. cxd5 Qxd5 3. g4 Bxg4 4. Qa4 Qxd2 { This time, black forgot to take with the bishop again and played Qxd2. Lucky for white, this one is easy. How can you punish that bishop? } 5. Kxd2 { Right! Now look where the bishop is headed...stuck on f1. All white has to do is delay black taking the queen. } Bxe2 6. Qxe8 Bxf1 { White's next move is tricky, but once you see how powerful it is you won't forget it! } 7. Qxf7 { That's right! There's not a win if you dump the queen right away. That's just something you'll have to remember. Don't worry, black can't do anything with the bishop. Find the win. Mess around with the black bishop and you'll see what I mean--no productive moves. } *
